Q7 – Diagnose, Redesign and Validate (13 Marks)
Bloom's Level: K5 – Evaluate
Selected solution: Q5 – Generic Ranking Component
For Q7, I have selected the Generic Leaderboard using Comparator from Q5.

The reason for selecting this solution is that the original implementation creates a new list and sorts all elements every time the ranking() method is called. If the leaderboard contains thousands of teams and users request rankings repeatedly, the same sorting work is performed unnecessarily.

The redesign will use a Cached Ranking Strategy. It will sort the teams only when the data changes and reuse the sorted result for subsequent ranking requests.

This changes the design based on the actual bottleneck instead of simply replacing one collection with another.

A. Diagnose the Bottleneck – 2 Marks
1. Original implementation
In Q5, the original ranking() method was:
List<T> ranking() {
    List<T> result = new ArrayList<>(items);
    result.sort(order);
    return result;
}


2. Identified limitations
1. Every call to ranking() creates a new ArrayList.
2. Every call copies all the existing team objects into the new list.
3. The entire list is sorted again, even when no team has been added or modified.
4. Sorting requires O(n log n) time.
5. Repeated requests increase execution time and temporary memory allocation.
3. Bottleneck analysis
Suppose a leaderboard contains 10,000 teams and the ranking is requested 100 times without changing the data.
