3. Revised pseudocode
START

Create original team list
Create cached ranking list
Set dirty = true

FUNCTION add(team):
    Add team to original list
    Set dirty = true

FUNCTION ranking():

    IF dirty is true:
        Copy original list
        Sort copied list using comparator
        Store sorted list in cache
        Set dirty = false

    Return unmodifiable cached ranking

STOP


4. What has changed?
Feature	Original design	Revised design
Sorting	Every request	Only after changes
Copying	Every request	Only when cache is rebuilt
Cache	Not available	Available
Dirty flag	Not available	Used
Correctness	Comparator	Same comparator
Additional memory	Temporary copy	Persistent cached copy

Trade-off: The redesigned system uses additional memory to store the cached ranking. Also, after every update, the next ranking request must rebuild the cache. This is beneficial when ranking requests are frequent and updates are relatively less frequent.
D. Predict Before Implementing – 1 Mark
Before implementation, the following behaviour is predicted:
1. The original implementation will sort the entire list for every ranking request.
2. The redesigned implementation will sort only once if no changes occur.
3. Repeated ranking requests will become faster.
4. When a new team is added, the cache will be invalidated and sorted again on the next request.
5. Both implementations will produce exactly the same ranking.
Prediction: With 10,000 teams and 100 ranking requests without updates, the redesigned solution should perform 1 sort instead of 100 sorts, a 99% reduction in sorting operations.
E. Implement and Validate the Redesign – 2 Marks
1. Complete Java implementation
The following program compares the original and redesigned solutions under the same conditions.

import java.util.*;

class Team {
    final String name;
    final int points;
    final int goalDiff;

    Team(String name, int points, int goalDiff) {
        this.name = name;
        this.points = points;
        this.goalDiff = goalDiff;
    }

    public String toString() {
        return name + "(" + points + "," + goalDiff + ")";
    }
}

// Original implementation
class OriginalLeaderboard {
    List<Team> items = new ArrayList<>();
    Comparator<Team> order;
    int sortCount = 0;

    OriginalLeaderboard(Comparator<Team> order) {
        this.order = order;
    }

    void add(Team t) {
        items.add(t);
    }

    List<Team> ranking() {
        List<Team> result = new ArrayList<>(items);
        result.sort(order);
        sortCount++;
        return result;
    }
}

// Redesigned implementation
class CachedLeaderboard {
    List<Team> items = new ArrayList<>();
    List<Team> cache;
    Comparator<Team> order;
    boolean dirty = true;
    int sortCount = 0;

    CachedLeaderboard(Comparator<Team> order) {
        this.order = order;
    }

    void add(Team t) {
        items.add(t);
        dirty = true;
    }

    List<Team> ranking() {

        if (dirty) {
            cache = new ArrayList<>(items);
            cache.sort(order);
            sortCount++;
            dirty = false;
        }

        return Collections.unmodifiableList(cache);
    }
}

public class Q7Demo {

    public static void main(String[] args) {

        Comparator<Team> byRank =
            Comparator.comparingInt((Team t) -> t.points)
            .reversed()
            .thenComparing(
                Comparator.comparingInt(
                    (Team t) -> t.goalDiff
                ).reversed()
            )
            .thenComparing(t -> t.name);

        OriginalLeaderboard original =
            new OriginalLeaderboard(byRank);

        CachedLeaderboard redesigned =
            new CachedLeaderboard(byRank);

        int n = 10000;
        int requests = 100;

        // Insert identical data into both systems
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            Team t = new Team(
                "Team" + i,
                i % 20,
                i % 10
            );

            original.add(t);
            redesigned.add(t);
        }

        // Original experiment
        long start = System.nanoTime();

        for (int i = 0; i < requests; i++) {
            original.ranking();
        }

        long originalTime =
            System.nanoTime() - start;

        // Redesigned experiment
        start = System.nanoTime();

        for (int i = 0; i < requests; i++) {
            redesigned.ranking();
        }

        long redesignedTime =
            System.nanoTime() - start;

        System.out.println("Original Sort Count: "
                           + original.sortCount);

        System.out.println("Redesigned Sort Count: "
                           + redesigned.sortCount);

        System.out.println("Original Time: "
                           + originalTime + " ns");

        System.out.println("Redesigned Time: "
                           + redesignedTime + " ns");

        // Check correctness
        System.out.println("Same Ranking: "
            + original.ranking().equals(
                redesigned.ranking()
            ));

        // Test cache invalidation
        redesigned.add(new Team("NewTeam", 25, 10));

        System.out.println("Updated Ranking: "
                           + redesigned.ranking().get(0));

        System.out.println("Sort Count After Update: "
                           + redesigned.sortCount);
    }
}



